367
00:41:31,720 --> 00:41:45,720
9B. 9B is a public hearing on the proposed creation of a tax increment financing district tentatively named TIF D8 pursuant to Alabama Code Section 11-99-1.

368
00:41:45,720 --> 00:41:48,720
And this is a public hearing only council members.

369
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:50,720
There will be no action taken tonight.

370
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:53,720
This is simply another step in the process of approving a TIF.

371
00:41:53,720 --> 00:41:57,720
Mr. Davis is here to make a presentation and then we will open the hearing.

372
00:41:57,720 --> 00:42:02,720
Thank you, Madam President. Shane Davis, Director of Urban Economic Development.

373
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:04,720
Good evening, council members.

374
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:07,720
You may recall the last city council meeting.

375
00:42:07,720 --> 00:42:17,720
You passed a resolution directing the administration to come back and present you a proposed TIF project plan.

376
00:42:17,720 --> 00:42:22,720
This project plan would be in Limestone County portion of Annex, Huntsville.

377
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:30,720
So we've been working for about three weeks to put this draft plan together and tonight we're proud to present it to you and the general public.

378
00:42:30,720 --> 00:42:42,720
So much like the recent TIF for downtown, I do want, especially for the public's sake, to just quickly give a little bit of background on TIF increment financing.

379
00:42:42,720 --> 00:42:54,720
Since 2000, the city of Huntsville has been very successful in establishing tax increment financing districts that are permitted by Alabama law to finance public infrastructure projects.

380
00:42:54,720 --> 00:42:57,720
The principle is very simple.

381
00:42:57,720 --> 00:43:02,720
You take future property tax revenues in a defined district.

382
00:43:02,720 --> 00:43:07,720
So think of property that is not currently developed, but as it develops, it creates a new tax base.

383
00:43:07,720 --> 00:43:11,720
That new tax base would fund public infrastructure.

384
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:17,720
That public infrastructure is put in ahead of time to induce or entice that private investment.

385
00:43:17,720 --> 00:43:22,720
We get routinely asked with the general public, is this a tax increase?

386
00:43:22,720 --> 00:43:24,720
It is absolutely not a tax increase.

387
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:28,720
The millage rate that you pay in Huntsville stays the same.

388
00:43:28,720 --> 00:43:33,720
That actually has to go by vote of the people to change property taxes.

389
00:43:33,720 --> 00:43:40,720
So this is just the way we would use those future property taxes to fund public infrastructure.

390
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:47,720
Lastly, the existing tax base within that district continues to go to the tax recipients as they do today.

391
00:43:47,720 --> 00:43:58,720
So we're not taking any existing revenue away from our general fund, in this case the Limestone County general fund, or any of the school systems within this tax district.

392
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:01,720
So they'll continue to get whatever they got last year.

393
00:44:01,720 --> 00:44:07,720
It will be any future revenues that would be created as a result of this infrastructure.

394
00:44:07,720 --> 00:44:13,720
I do want to point out this proposed TIF VIII district is different than some of the others.

395
00:44:13,720 --> 00:44:19,720
This would be our third district under the major 21st Century Manufacturing Act.

396
00:44:19,720 --> 00:44:29,720
TIF VI and VII, TIF VI has closed, was the first 21st Century Manufacturing Zone TIF district.

397
00:44:29,720 --> 00:44:36,720
The Mazda Toyota Manufacturing Project brought before you in the Limestone County Commission, TIF VII.

398
00:44:36,720 --> 00:44:45,720
That is active and really moved the needle out there with public infrastructure and roads and utilities and the things.

399
00:44:45,720 --> 00:44:57,720
And through those two TIF districts, what we have created out in that area is over $3 billion of private investment that's now on the tax rolls and over 14,000 new jobs.

400
00:44:57,720 --> 00:45:04,720
So the proposed TIF VIII district would be created under the major 21st Century Manufacturing Zone Act.

401
00:45:04,720 --> 00:45:12,720
And the TIF VIII district would designate for the future Eli Lilly project that's recently announced and would get under construction sometime next year.

402
00:45:12,720 --> 00:45:18,720
That would be our designated manufacturing zone under this Act with the TIF.

403
00:45:18,720 --> 00:45:23,720
You've got to designate a manufacturing zone and we'll get into that momentarily.

404
00:45:24,720 --> 00:45:26,720
So let's get into the actual project plan.

405
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:30,720
Just wanted to provide that background, the differences, and also the general public.

406
00:45:30,720 --> 00:45:36,720
This is nothing about any type of tax increase to anyone.

407
00:45:36,720 --> 00:45:46,720
So the project area, you can see kind of dashed in the black dashed area and shaded in the light shading, would consist of just over 9,000 acres.

408
00:45:46,720 --> 00:45:55,720
This would be very similar in size to TIF VII that we did that's to the north and actually goes all the way to I-65.

409
00:45:55,720 --> 00:46:09,720
The boundary, generally speaking, would be Old Highway 20 to the north, Swancott Road to the south, County Line Road to the east, there at the airport you see on the right hand side of the screen,

410
00:46:09,720 --> 00:46:17,720
and Prior Road to the west, and Prior Road is just west of Exit 3 on the south side of I-565.

411
00:46:17,720 --> 00:46:22,720
So what would the project plan look like?

412
00:46:22,720 --> 00:46:35,720
So as a result of the city's public infrastructure investments, the proposed TIF VIII plan would capture future property tax millages from future new development or redevelopment properties within that area I just showed you.

413
00:46:35,720 --> 00:46:38,720
So what would we capture of that tax base?

414
00:46:38,720 --> 00:46:49,720
It would be 54 mills total, 35 mills of the city of Huntsville, only 5.5 mills of the education portion, 13.5 mills of Limestone County portion of the overall millage.

415
00:46:49,720 --> 00:46:55,720
The overall millage of this area for Huntsville is 60.5 mills.

416
00:46:55,720 --> 00:47:00,720
So there would be 6.5 mills that would not be captured in this TIF District.

417
00:47:00,720 --> 00:47:12,720
Upon the creation of TIF District 8, the full implementation of the proposed public investments, we certainly anticipate that it would yield significant new private investment in these areas.

418
00:47:12,720 --> 00:47:16,720
If I go back to this map, if you look, it's predominantly undeveloped.

419
00:47:16,720 --> 00:47:29,720
That is the purpose of a TIF, is to induce or entice, especially under the 21st Century Manufacturing Act, is go make those public investments such that you will entice new private investment to add to the tax rolls.

420
00:47:29,720 --> 00:47:35,720
That new investment helps our schools, it helps our general fund, it certainly helps Limestone County's general fund in the future.

421
00:47:35,720 --> 00:47:49,720
As a result, preliminary modeling suggests that upon completion of these investments that I'll go through momentarily, we'll produce a new tax base of somewhere between 20 and 25 million dollars annually.

422
00:47:49,720 --> 00:47:57,720
That certainly would get distributed between the City of Huntsville, our educational partners, the way the millage is broken out, and Limestone County Commission.

423
00:47:57,720 --> 00:48:00,720
So let's go through the list.

424
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:08,720
I apologize for the font kind of not aligning on this computer, but it's a pretty long list.

425
00:48:08,720 --> 00:48:18,720
It's very similar to TIF 7 in that with the Eli Lilly project, there's an opportunity for us to get a lot done in this TIF District.

426
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:27,720
So Greenbrier Parkway and Greenbrier Road improvements at a cost of 8 million dollars will go into a map and show you these locations momentarily.

427
00:48:27,720 --> 00:48:34,720
Interstate I-565 Exit 3 improvements at Alabama Highway 20 at 15 million dollars.

428
00:48:34,720 --> 00:48:46,720
With the amount of growth that we've had in industrial recruitment out there, we have a need with the way shift work happens in this Limestone-Greenbrier area.

429
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:55,720
Exit 3 in the mornings backs up as people are coming from Huntsville westbound to go to these 14,000 jobs.

430
00:48:55,720 --> 00:48:59,720
That's what we wanted. We want our community to take advantage of the jobs we created.

431
00:48:59,720 --> 00:49:05,720
So this would make improvements to alleviate that congestion at I-565 at Exit 3.

432
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:12,720
Swancott Road widening, this would go from Exit 3 south to Bowling Boulevard to the airport.

433
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:26,720
It's an area we believe will see significant growth, but this project also helps Eli Lilly and others to have a better route to the intermodal facility for the air cargo at our airport.

434
00:49:26,720 --> 00:49:30,720
It takes traffic off the interstate, takes truck traffic in that manner.

435
00:49:30,720 --> 00:49:37,720
It was one of the commitments for Eli Lilly, is to have a more direct access route or a secondary route.

436
00:49:37,720 --> 00:49:41,720
If there's a wreck on the interstate, it's pretty much a single point of failure.

437
00:49:41,720 --> 00:49:44,720
So again, it's heavy on transportation.

438
00:49:44,720 --> 00:49:46,720
Prior road improvements, we'll get into that.

439
00:49:46,720 --> 00:49:51,720
A portion of that is a relocation of Prior Road and one is an improvement of Prior Road.

440
00:49:51,720 --> 00:49:53,720
You'll see an amount momentarily.

441
00:49:53,720 --> 00:49:59,720
In other words, people's road improvements, so that runs east-west off Swancott Road to Prior Road.

442
00:49:59,720 --> 00:50:03,720
And that will be in support of a new K Elementary School.

443
00:50:03,720 --> 00:50:05,720
It is number 8 at $40 million.

444
00:50:06,720 --> 00:50:16,720
County Line Road relocation upgrades, that would move County Line Road from its current location from I-565 south to Bowling Boulevard west.

