626
01:07:55,720 --> 01:07:56,720
Yes.

627
01:07:56,720 --> 01:08:01,720
So the two that have to vote are deferred tax recipients.

628
01:08:01,720 --> 01:08:05,720
So those are people who assess taxes and collect them.

629
01:08:05,720 --> 01:08:09,720
So our educational partners, both in the county and the city, do not assess.

630
01:08:09,720 --> 01:08:11,720
They do not place a millage on property.

631
01:08:11,720 --> 01:08:16,720
Both you and a county does that, certainly the state of Alabama.

632
01:08:16,720 --> 01:08:22,720
We collect and then we disperse by the millage that we set up that goes to education.

633
01:08:22,720 --> 01:08:26,720
So the two bodies that would have to vote on this TIF would be you,

634
01:08:26,720 --> 01:08:29,720
the city council and the Limestone County Commission.

635
01:08:29,720 --> 01:08:39,720
Now, to answer Councilman Cleen's question is one, the existing tax base that this district is producing today

636
01:08:39,720 --> 01:08:43,720
continues to go to everyone that the millage gets cut up.

637
01:08:43,720 --> 01:08:45,720
That goes to really four bodies.

638
01:08:45,720 --> 01:08:48,720
It goes to City Hall, General Fund.

639
01:08:48,720 --> 01:08:51,720
It goes to the Limestone County Commission.

640
01:08:51,720 --> 01:08:54,720
Limestone County Schools and Huntsville City Schools.

641
01:08:54,720 --> 01:08:59,720
Both the Limestone County Commission sends whatever millage that they've got designated

642
01:08:59,720 --> 01:09:01,720
to go to their school system just as you do.

643
01:09:01,720 --> 01:09:05,720
But you and the Limestone County Commission are the two deferred tax recipients.

644
01:09:05,720 --> 01:09:11,720
You assess taxes or put before and collect those.

645
01:09:11,720 --> 01:09:14,720
So one, it's not a tax increase.

646
01:09:14,720 --> 01:09:19,720
Two, we are not taking any existing revenues away from education,

647
01:09:19,720 --> 01:09:22,720
nor City of Huntsville General Fund or Limestone County General Fund.

648
01:09:22,720 --> 01:09:29,720
It is only the future revenues that would not most likely be seen without these investments.

649
01:09:29,720 --> 01:09:32,720
These are very rural two-lane roads.

650
01:09:32,720 --> 01:09:35,720
