01:20:46,720 --> 01:20:58,720
People with hearing loss rely on hearing aids and other technology to be independent and to participate in their communities, to work, to go to school, and to testify at city council meetings.

819
01:20:58,720 --> 01:21:02,720
For most of us, a hearing aid is not a luxury or a want.

820
01:21:02,720 --> 01:21:06,720
It is a fundamental necessity for quality of life.

821
01:21:07,720 --> 01:21:12,720
Hearing aids last about three to five years on average, so they're not a long-term investment.

822
01:21:12,720 --> 01:21:20,720
Many people with hearing loss experience decline over time so that replacements are needed sooner than that five-year frame.

823
01:21:20,720 --> 01:21:24,720
Hearing aids are not covered by Medicare and most insurance companies.

824
01:21:24,720 --> 01:21:29,720
It is an out-of-pocket expense and in this case it's taxed.

825
01:21:29,720 --> 01:21:33,720
They range in price from $99 to over $8,000.

826
01:21:33,720 --> 01:21:36,720
I just ordered a new hearing aid on Tuesday.

827
01:21:36,720 --> 01:21:40,720
It will cost me $1,950.

828
01:21:40,720 --> 01:21:48,720
The tax on that is $78 and that's small in terms of the bigger price, but it's also a big strain, especially these days.

829
01:21:48,720 --> 01:21:52,720
I am paying a tax for something I fundamentally need.

830
01:21:52,720 --> 01:21:54,720
There's no choice.

831
01:21:54,720 --> 01:22:02,720
If I want to be independent and participate in my community, this is the only hearing aid that works with the technology that I need.

832
01:22:02,720 --> 01:22:08,720
For many in our community, you are believing them of a tax burden of between $20 and $40.

833
01:22:08,720 --> 01:22:16,720
There's small loss of revenue for the city and a major relief for many of our citizens who have retired or are on limited incomes.

834
01:22:16,720 --> 01:22:26,720
I would like each of you to consider that continuing this tax, you are taxing an item that is absolutely necessary and absolutely critical for some of our citizens.

835
01:22:26,720 --> 01:22:34,720
It is certainly enough of a budget consideration that next time I'll drive up to Madison City to buy a hearing aid where they have repealed the tax.

836
01:22:34,720 --> 01:22:39,720
Many cities across the state are doing this and I hope that Huntsville would be a leader.

837
01:22:39,720 --> 01:22:41,720
Thank you so much.

838
01:22:41,720 --> 01:22:42,720
Thank you.

839
01:22:42,720 --> 01:22:45,720
Ms. Higgins, the next person to speak will be Forrest Satterfield.

840
01:22:45,720 --> 01:22:47,720
Is Mr. Satterfield here?

841
01:22:47,720 --> 01:22:49,720
Forrest Satterfield?

842
01:22:49,720 --> 01:22:51,720
He is not here.

843
01:22:52,720 --> 01:22:55,720
Then we will, that will, oh.

844
01:22:59,720 --> 01:23:01,720
Hey y'all.

845
01:23:01,720 --> 01:23:03,720
Your name and address for the record.

846
01:23:03,720 --> 01:23:09,720
Forrest Satterfield, Constellation, so that's 740 Constellation Place Drive over behind the VBC.

847
01:23:09,720 --> 01:23:11,720
Very good, thank you sir.

848
01:23:11,720 --> 01:23:16,720
I should have gone before Susan, she did a much better job at that.

849
01:23:16,720 --> 01:23:23,720
What I will say is that hearing loss is something that is not something that people choose to have.

850
01:23:23,720 --> 01:23:31,720
And if we were to tax these people, the total income that I am aware of is between $100,000 and $150,000.

851
01:23:31,720 --> 01:23:38,720
That benefit to the city is small and yet as Susan so eloquently put, is great to the individuals.

852
01:23:38,720 --> 01:23:45,720
And so I would advocate that we take away this tax so that it does not impact people who are in addition to paying for these hearing aids,

853
01:23:45,720 --> 01:23:50,720
paying for the batteries, paying for the procedures, paying for the continued upkeep.

854
01:23:50,720 --> 01:23:58,720
You know, as was once again said so well by Susan, these are things that really do add up for the people of Huntsville.

855
01:23:58,720 --> 01:23:59,720
Thank you.

856
01:23:59,720 --> 01:24:00,720
Thank you sir.

