881
01:26:42,720 --> 01:26:45,720
The people who were here were from all over the world.

882
01:26:45,720 --> 01:26:51,720
It was an international crowd and they couldn't say enough nice things about the city except where it was hot.

883
01:26:51,720 --> 01:26:57,720
But to each of you, especially to the chamber, thank you for the work that you did.

884
01:26:57,720 --> 01:27:00,720
Thank you for what you did for our community.

885
01:27:00,720 --> 01:27:09,720
As I told someone, I said, you know, this really is an exercise of showing that we have a heart and a big, big heart.

886
01:27:09,720 --> 01:27:11,720
So thank you.

887
01:27:11,720 --> 01:27:12,720
Thank you, Mayor Battle.

888
01:27:12,720 --> 01:27:16,720
We'll go on to Councilmember Cummings and hear first from Councilmember Bill Cleen.

889
01:27:16,720 --> 01:27:18,720
Thank you, Madam President.

890
01:27:19,720 --> 01:27:25,720
One of the concerns I want to express, especially as we start pivoting into a new fiscal year,

891
01:27:25,720 --> 01:27:33,720
is what seems to have been a pattern which unfortunately had taken place in numerous streets,

892
01:27:33,720 --> 01:27:40,720
I think not just within the district I represent, but I think in other streets that were being resurfaced in other parts of the city.

893
01:27:41,720 --> 01:27:50,720
There's a process where streets, for example, let me use Holiday Drive as an example, is prepped before resurfacing takes place.

894
01:27:50,720 --> 01:28:00,720
The contractor and the people come in, they kind of mill the asphalt down, they fix the curb and have everything all prepped up.

895
01:28:00,720 --> 01:28:07,720
And then there's a second contractor that comes in who basically takes over and does the fun part,

896
01:28:07,720 --> 01:28:10,720
laying out the asphalt with the results that people like to see.

897
01:28:10,720 --> 01:28:20,720
There's been a process, it's been a problem rather, where Holiday Drive, for example, spent at least seven months where it was torn up

898
01:28:20,720 --> 01:28:25,720
and the residents on it had to live on it, go through the dust, slow down.

899
01:28:25,720 --> 01:28:29,720
Occasionally there would be a windshield that would get hit with the pea gravel.

900
01:28:29,720 --> 01:28:39,720
And they would have to wait and we would still not get a satisfactory response from the public works director about when the asphalt contractor would be coming.

901
01:28:39,720 --> 01:28:49,720
I'm using as an example, Harwood, Holiday, similar example, had a long waiting period.

902
01:28:49,720 --> 01:28:59,720
Homewood Drive basically went through being milled in the fall and then not being resurfaced until the wintertime came.

903
01:28:59,720 --> 01:29:03,720
Eustis, it's still like a work in progress.

904
01:29:03,720 --> 01:29:14,720
But I'd like to see if there's some way we can either get with this public works director or whoever takes charge to have something lined up where the contractors know

905
01:29:14,720 --> 01:29:23,720
and they are bound by contract and whatever it takes to make it happen where there's a reasonable period of time where the prepping is done

906
01:29:23,720 --> 01:29:29,720
and then after the prepping is done, shortly thereafter the asphalting would take place.

907
01:29:29,720 --> 01:29:38,720
By contrast, I hate to say this, but in our backyard over here on Church Street, we had something similar where it was milled, it was prepped.

908
01:29:38,720 --> 01:29:47,720
And then very shortly after, then the asphalt would come in and that would minimize the inconvenience that the citizens had to go through.

909
01:29:47,720 --> 01:29:49,720
But I think this is a problem.

910
01:29:49,720 --> 01:30:00,720
We've got a new fiscal year coming up and I think that's a good time just to get a process in place, make sure it's going to be followed, make sure that if somebody's going to do business with the city,

911
01:30:01,720 --> 01:30:05,720
that they have a certain window of time that they're supposed to do their job.

912
01:30:05,720 --> 01:30:18,720
And then the next contractor has a window where he's supposed to do his job and follow through because these resurfacing, we like doing them because they're supposed to be a benefit for our neighborhoods and for the people who live on them.

913
01:30:18,720 --> 01:30:26,720
But for many of the people there, very, very unhappy and a lot of inconvenience that took place for those folks.

914
01:30:26,720 --> 01:30:33,720
So just something I wanted to throw out for Public Works to do during the upcoming, hopefully the new fiscal year.

915
01:30:33,720 --> 01:30:37,720
That's all, Madam President. Oh, one other, no, that's all. Thank you.

916
01:30:37,720 --> 01:30:41,720
Thank you, Mr. Kling. We'll now hear from Councilmember David Little.

917
01:30:41,720 --> 01:30:50,720
Thank you, Madam President. I'd like to thank our Engineering, Public Works, Traffic Department and HPD on being responsive to some citizen concerns these last few weeks.

918
01:30:51,720 --> 01:30:58,720
And then also, most everybody knows next month is Community Planning Month, National Community Planning Month.

919
01:30:58,720 --> 01:31:06,720
And accordingly, we're going to be doing a meeting out in the Hampton Cove area mid to late October to talk about the good things we're working on out there.

920
01:31:06,720 --> 01:31:08,720
That's all I've got. Thank you.

921
01:31:08,720 --> 01:31:09,720
Thank you, Mr. Wood.

922
